      "description": "This course consists of preparatory assignments in readings and a written study plan, followed by a five to seven-day residential programme in a selected country or economy outside of Hong Kong and concluded with a written report and oral presentation. The residential programme will include site visits to state enterprises, joint ventures and manufacturing facilities as well as lectures, seminars and discussions with local and international company executives. The goal in taking learning sessions abroad is for Master’s students to expose to a wide spectrum of issues related to business operations, management and innovation in different nations and/ or regions. Through discussions with local government officials, managers and academics, trade, economics, finance, market, ventures, management practices, technologies, as well as geopolitics and social issues are highlighted.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "For students in Master of Accountancy; MBA; MSc Business Analytics; MSc Finance; MSc Info & Technology Mgt; MSc Management; MSc Marketing; MSc Real Estate; MSc Sustainable Global Business; MSc Aviation Management; or MSc Leadership for Experience Economy",
      "course_attributes": "",
      "academic_career": "Postgraduate - Taught",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Field Studies/Field-trip",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Div of Business Administration",
      "academic_org": "Div of Business Administration",
      "learning_outcomes": "Upon completion of the course, students will gain a basic understanding of the current business practices and related issues in the visiting country, economic regions, unions or association of nations.",
      "course_syllabus": "(1) Economic, political and cultural environment of the visiting country/ region\n\n(2) General business environment in the visiting country/ region\n\n(3) Business opportunities and challenges of local business\n\n(4) Local business practices",
